<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valencia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valencia is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, surrounded by a fertile irrigated plain known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">huerta</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> it was an important city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. The Almoravid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> profiles cite the irrigated huertas of Valencia among the most productive agricultural zones of their Iberian territories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valencia.jpg" alt="Valencia" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boris Dzhingarov · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malvarrosa_Beach,_Valencia,_Spain_(29812271043).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
